course: dictionary
lesson: 11688
title: Attainable goals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attainable means something you can reach or achieve if you work at it. Break the word into parts: attain means to reach or get, and -able means you are able to do it. So an attainable goal is one you really can reach.
explain: «Reading ten pages a night is an attainable goal for Ava.» Ava can do this with practice, so the goal is possible. To check a word like this, ask: could I really reach this with effort? If yes, it is attainable.
explain: Attainable does not mean easy. A goal can be hard and still attainable. The opposite is unattainable: «Flying to the Moon by lunchtime is unattainable for anyone.» That goal cannot be reached, so it is not attainable.
fact: Attainable means possible to reach or achieve.
fact: Attainable can also mean possible to get, as in «Tickets are still attainable.»
fact: An attainable goal is challenging but possible to reach.
fact: Teachers often use SMART goals: specific, measurable, achievable, realistic and timed.
fact: The opposite of attainable is unattainable.
exercise: «Ava wants to read ten pages a day, which is an attainable goal.» What does attainable mean here? | Very expensive | Impossible to reach | Easy to lose | *Possible to reach
exercise: «Tickets for the show are still attainable.» What does attainable mean in this sentence? | Impossible to get | Lost in the post | *Possible to get | Sold out forever
exercise: Which word is the opposite of attainable? | Achievable | *Unattainable | Possible | Reachable
test: Which goal is attainable for a child your age? | Be the fastest runner in the world by Monday | *Read one chapter of a book each night | Fly to the Moon by lunchtime
test: Mia says her goal is unattainable. What does she mean? | *She thinks it is not possible to reach | She has already reached it | She thinks it is easy to reach | She has only just started it
exam: «Seats for the concert are still attainable, so book one today.» What does attainable mean in this sentence? | *Possible to get | Too loud | Painted in bright colours | Very old
